.TH EMULSIFY 1 "2026-08-22" "emulsify 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
emulsify \- viscosity-based merge compatibility analysis and nearest-neighbour consolidation planning
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B emulsify
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Emulsify treats forks as fluids ranked by viscosity (the inverse of
measured compatibility with the host) and consolidates them at their
nearest compatible architectural state. Every fork is scored across
nine dimensions \(em api, types, dependencies, architecture, behaviour,
tests, ownership, lineage, abstraction \(em and classified into one of
four states:
.TP
.B mix
direct bind into the host (low viscosity)
.TP
.B emulsify
bind through a consolidation adapter
.TP
.B suspend
keep independently maintained behind an interface boundary
.TP
.B reject
immiscible; do not merge directly
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI analyze " HOST FORK..."
Measure the viscosity of each fork against the host; prints a summary
table and per-fork dimension breakdown.
.TP
.BI plan " HOST FORK..."
Produce an ordered nearest-neighbour consolidation plan.
.TP
.BI graph " HOST FORK..."
Print the full pairwise compatibility matrix.
.TP
.BI analyze\-snapshots " HOST\-SNAPSHOT FORK\-SNAPSHOT..."
Like
.BR analyze ,
but reads bound-snapshot/v1 JSON files produced by a snapshotter instead of
scanning source directories.
.TP
.BI plan\-snapshots " HOST\-SNAPSHOT FORK\-SNAPSHOT..."
Like
.BR plan ,
but reads bound-snapshot/v1 JSON files.
.TP
.BI graph\-snapshots " HOST\-SNAPSHOT FORK\-SNAPSHOT..."
Like
.BR graph ,
but reads bound-snapshot/v1 JSON files.
.TP
.B init
Write an example
.B emulsify.toml
in the current directory. Refuses to overwrite unless
.B \-\-force
is given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON instead of text.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Load configuration from
.IR PATH .
When absent, ./emulsify.toml is used if it exists; otherwise defaults.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error.
.SH FILES
./emulsify.toml \(em optional configuration: [weights] per dimension,
[thresholds] mix/emulsify/suspend compatibility bands.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Measure two forks against a host and print the per-dimension breakdown:
.nf

emulsify analyze ./host ./fork-a ./fork-b
.fi
.TP
Emit a machine-readable consolidation plan:
.nf

emulsify plan ./host ./fork-a --json
.fi
.TP
Print the pairwise compatibility matrix for three codebases:
.nf

emulsify graph ./host ./fork-a ./fork-b
.fi
.TP
Analyze from pre-built bound-snapshot/v1 JSON files instead of directories:
.nf

emulsify analyze-snapshots host.snap.json fork.snap.json
.fi
.TP
Write an example configuration file in the current directory:
.nf

emulsify init
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
git(1)
